                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e8c3d307-80be-485a-873f-2a37a7e8bd83",
                        "entry_id": "3505e25b-92b3-3d2d-9e42-002ba9657d7a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "шелкови́цах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18f4de82-d841-3d90-933c-18fe2dc7ca1a",
                        "entry_id": "3505e25b-92b3-3d2d-9e42-002ba9657d7a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан. род растений семейства тутовых"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d822638-2847-4808-829a-ac6e9fac4397",
                                "sense_id": "18f4de82-d841-3d90-933c-18fe2dc7ca1a",
                                "text": "По всему саду, особенно у терраски, в огромных кадках дивные олеандры, а над самым обрывом — старая шелковица."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d479aad-0320-4f20-9a4b-eeeeb6a85f4f",
                                "sense_id": "18f4de82-d841-3d90-933c-18fe2dc7ca1a",
                                "text": "Шелковица возле дома дяди Тараса была такая огромная и плодоносная, что до отвала накармливала всех детей нашего двора."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee0a04cc-be78-3eab-8535-808a968f495e",
                        "entry_id": "3505e25b-92b3-3d2d-9e42-002ba9657d7a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. плоды шелковицы, употребляемые в пищу"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11c27d09-b1af-4e62-a0d0-a2065a51e27c",
                                "sense_id": "ee0a04cc-be78-3eab-8535-808a968f495e",
                                "text": "Лазили мы с ним и на деревья есть шелковицу."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6580a9b1-21ae-4713-bf9a-3fab875d571b",
                                "sense_id": "ee0a04cc-be78-3eab-8535-808a968f495e",
                                "text": "Зачерпнув из котелка полную горсть шелковицы, головой указывает мне на писаря."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "168906c3-640a-4b2e-8ce4-dc5d637495f2",
                        "source_entry_id": "3505e25b-92b3-3d2d-9e42-002ba9657d7a",
                        "target_lang_word": "mulberry",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mulberry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce70747f-2a3a-3497-8a7e-02457ed09e2f",
                                        "entry_id": "70d069c7-3605-3cc0-9532-6c4455590351",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several trees, of the genus Morus, having edible fruits."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf8dd77c-3a0c-424c-9d9b-1884936eb73f",
                                                "sense_id": "ce70747f-2a3a-3497-8a7e-02457ed09e2f",
                                                "text": "Different qualities of the Mulberry. Among the different species of the Mulberry, it is ascertained that the Italian, (Morus italica) is eaten by the silk worm, with eager appetite. It's fruit is very small, and of a pale rose colour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffb074a0-af4f-4953-aea8-f9e0b792c32a",
                                                "sense_id": "ce70747f-2a3a-3497-8a7e-02457ed09e2f",
                                                "text": "Beyond the south end of the lake, the route lies across the plain of Lombardy, where the mulberry trees are evidence of the silk industry."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41ca2cbf-2d77-3a5c-8024-05cb1abce165",
                                        "entry_id": "70d069c7-3605-3cc0-9532-6c4455590351",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The fruit of this tree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a34876c-ee2f-45c5-98c1-cba25b990656",
                                                "sense_id": "41ca2cbf-2d77-3a5c-8024-05cb1abce165",
                                                "text": "You can also make good jam with mulberries, and they taste great cooked or mixed together with other fruits. Mulberries are rich in sugar with moderate amounts of vitamin C. Their rich colours are a sign that they contain high levels of […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e645dc3-8aec-3257-8e0d-a4bd8c1c8213",
                                        "entry_id": "70d069c7-3605-3cc0-9532-6c4455590351",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dark purple colour tinted with red."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
